  "status": "Appeal Received",
  "description": "Double Storey Side/ Part Rear Extension",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of mass, siting and design, would be an undesirable addition which would result in a complex roof form, would be overly dominant and would detract from existing positive features of the street scene.&nbsp;It would fail to respect or reflect the character and appearance of the original dwelling, the terrace row, and the wider Becontree Estate, causing harm to each of these. The proposal would appear&nbsp;out-of-keeping with the local distinctiveness and historic character of the&nbsp;Becontree Estate, causing detrimental harm to the non-designated heritage asset. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that developments are sympathetic to local character:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024) Policies&nbsp;D4 and HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021) The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012) Policies SPP6, SP2, DMD1, DMD4&nbsp;and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
  ],
